1329	1332	1334	1340	a hard - featured dame of fifty	83	" Goodwives , "
1342	1436	1334	1340	a hard - featured dame of fifty	83	" I 'll tell ye a piece of my mind . It would be greatly for the public behoof if we women , being of mature age and church - members in good repute , should have the handling of such malefactresses as this Hester Prynne . What think ye , gossips ? If the hussy stood up for judgment before us five , that are now here in a knot together , would she come off with such a sentence as the worshipful magistrates have awarded ? Marry , I trow not . "
1437	1441	1334	1340	a hard - featured dame of fifty	83	" People say , "
1445	1473	1334	1340	a hard - featured dame of fifty	83	" that the Reverend Master Dimmesdale , her godly pastor , takes it very grievously to heart that such a scandal should have come upon his congregation . "
1474	1492	1334	1340	a hard - featured dame of fifty	83	" The magistrates are God - fearing gentlemen , but merciful overmuch -- that is a truth , "
1499	1583	1334	1340	a hard - featured dame of fifty	83	" At the very least , they should have put the brand of a hot iron on Hester Prynne 's forehead . Madame Hester would have winced at that , I warrant me . But she -- the naughty baggage -- little will she care what they put upon the bodice of her gown ! Why , look you , she may cover it with a brooch , or such like heathenish adornment , and so walk the streets as brave as ever ! "
1584	1589	1595	1597	a young wife	84	" Ah , but , "
1606	1627	1595	1597	a young wife	84	" let her cover the mark as she will , the pang of it will be always in her heart . "
1628	1652	1654	1655	another female	86	" What do we talk of marks and brands , whether on the bodice of her gown or the flesh of her forehead ? "
1672	1732	1654	1655	another female	86	" This woman has brought shame upon us all , and ought to die ; is there not law for it ? Truly there is , both in the Scripture and the statute - book . Then let the magistrates , who have made it of no effect , thank themselves if their own wives and daughters go astray . "
1733	1740	1742	1746	a man in the crowd	88	" Mercy on us , goodwife ! "
1748	1796	1742	1746	a man in the crowd	88	" is there no virtue in woman , save what springs from a wholesome fear of the gallows ? That is the hardest word yet ! Hush now , gossips for the lock is turning in the prison - door , and here comes Mistress Prynne herself . "
